     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe. Metformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That's twice the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day (about 850 mg TID) for immediate-release metformin. A single 1700 mg dose is also above the usual maximum per dose. At this level the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity is high, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nWhich of these did you intend?\n- **850 mg PO TID with meals**, which is 2,550 mg/day, the usual maximum.\n- **1700 mg total daily**, for example 850 mg PO BID with meals.\n- **Some other dose.** If 5,100 mg/day is really what you want, tell me and I'll enter it with a note recording that you confirmed it.\n\nOnce you confirm, I'll enter the order right away."
      }
